# Changelog and version

Any change that will be committed, pushed, or included in a PR must update **both** root `CHANGELOG.md` and `workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml` in the **same** change as the code. Do not leave shippable work only under `[Unreleased]`.

Keep [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) form and [SemVer](https://semver.org/). Newest version first. An empty `## [Unreleased]` section stays on top.

## When

Update version notes when the work:

- Fixes rendering, import, tessellation, transforms, picking, selection, or viewport behavior
- Adds or changes a user-facing command, UI, settings, or `--import-only` output
- Changes a public crate API or build/runtime packaging

Skip only formatting-only edits, comment-only edits, and uncommitted plan files. `.cursor/rules` that change project process **do** get a changelog bullet.

## Version bump (0.x)

- **Patch** (`0.2.0` → `0.2.1`): fixes and robustness with no new user-facing capability
- **Minor** (`0.1.0` → `0.2.0`): new commands, UI, or selection/rendering features
- Never reuse a released version number; match `CHANGELOG.md` to `Cargo.toml`

## How to write entries

Move new bullets into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` (today’s date). Start with a verb: `Fix`, `Add`, `Change`, `Remove`. Say **why it matters**, not the file list. Group under `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Fixed`, or `### Removed`. Name DWG/entity types in caps (`LWPOLYLINE`, `INSERT`).

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

## [0.2.1] - 2026-09-03

### Fixed
- Correct LWPOLYLINE bulge sign so positive bulge is CCW in world XY.
```

```toml
# Cargo.toml — must match the new changelog version
[workspace.package]
version = "0.2.1"
```
